{%- comment -%}
  fye-buybox-sides — the side-diamond chooser, for trilogy rings only.

  Rendered by main-product after fye-buybox-centre. Side stones are a TRILOGY
  concern and nothing else — Ed, 31/08/2026.

  ── THE GATE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

      section.settings.enable_side_diamonds   unticked on product.complete.json
      tag "Trilogy Ring"
      fye.side_stones.code                    {"cut":"Pear","pair_ct":0.2,"code":"PE-020"}

  All three. The 8 tension trilogies have no side_stones metafield and behave
  like any other ring, which is correct — their sides are structural.

  A COMPLETE trilogy carries the metafield AND sits on product.complete.json,
  so its panel is off: the sides are already set and paid for. The template is
  the authority, not the metafield. Getting that backwards prices the ring
  twice.

  ── NOTHING IS SELECTED ON LOAD ───────────────────────────────────────────

  Ed, 31/08/2026. No mode card and NO QUALITY CHIP carries `is-on`. Live
  preselects both — the "Required" card and the F/G VS chip — so a trilogy
  could be bought with a grade nobody chose. fye-ui.js must block add to cart
  until a mode is picked, and until a chip is picked when the mode is
  "Required".

  ── THE THREE CHOICES DO NOT OVERLAP ──────────────────────────────────────

  Ed, 31/08/2026. On a trilogy with diamond-set shoulders the customer picks:

    · the centre diamond          its own cart line, its own price
    · the side diamond quality    its own cart line, its own price  (this file)
    · the shoulder diamond grade  the "Diamond Quality" variant option, which
                                  with Metal sets the VARIANT price

  So the ordinary quality selector stays on screen and keeps working. Live
  hides it on any trilogy with a side_stones metafield and locks the ring to
  its cheapest grade (its W333); that is NOT ported, because on a set-shoulder
  ring it removes a real choice the customer is entitled to make.

  ── WHY THE SIDES ARE A SEPARATE LINE ─────────────────────────────────────

  Ed's call, 20/08/2026: ring price and side-stone price must be independent.
  The four choices are variants of four hidden add-on products, matched by SKU
  tail against this ring's `code`, and their PRICES ARE READ LIVE off those
  products. Repricing side stones is four product edits and touches no ring.

  ── PROPERTY NAMES ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  "Side Diamonds" and "Setting service" follow the centre panel's pattern.
  UNVERIFIED against live's own keys — live's side-stone properties sit in the
  part of product-block.js past the readable limit. Confirm with Ed before
  go-live: a mismatched key means the workshop does not see the instruction.

  Parameters: product, settings (the section's)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = settings
  assign p = product
  assign sides = p.metafields.fye.side_stones.value

  assign code = sides.code
  assign cut = sides.cut | downcase
  assign pair_ct = sides.pair_ct

  assign want = '-' | append: code

  comment
    "Supply your own" needs BOTH a fee variant and a fee price. Without the
    price the card would advertise the service at £0.00, which is worse than
    not offering it — so the card hides itself until both are set, the same
    way the engraving control does. The fee figure is outstanding from Ed.
  endcomment
  assign has_sides_fee = false
  if s.sides_fee_variant_id != blank and s.sides_fee_price_pennies > 0
    assign has_sides_fee = true
  endif

  comment
    The four add-on products, handle*display, exactly as live hardcodes them.
    A handle that does not resolve simply renders no chip — a missing add-on
    product must not take add-to-cart down with it.

    all_products is capped at 20 unique handles per page. Four here, and the
    plain-ring metal switcher (up to 8) never runs on a trilogy, so there is
    headroom. Anything else added to this page counts against the same cap.
  endcomment
  assign addons = 'trilogy-side-diamonds-devvs*D/E VVS,trilogy-side-diamonds-fgvs*F/G VS,trilogy-side-diamonds-gsi*G Si,trilogy-side-diamonds-lab*Lab-grown D VVS' | split: ','
-%}

<div class="pdp__choose"
     data-fye-sides
     data-fee-variant="{{ s.sides_fee_variant_id }}"
     data-fee-price="{{ s.sides_fee_price_pennies | default: 0 }}">

  <p class="pdp__label">{{ s.sides_heading | default: 'Side diamonds' }}</p>
  <p class="pdp__choosenote">
    A matched pair of {{ cut }} diamonds, {{ pair_ct }}ct combined, one set either side of the centre stone.
  </p>

  <div class="pdp__modes" role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{ s.sides_heading | default: 'Side diamonds' | escape }}">
    <button type="button"
            class="pdp__mode"
            role="radio"
            aria-checked="false"
            data-fye-sides-mode="required">
      <span class="pdp__modetitle">{{ s.sides_required_label | default: 'Choose a pair' }}</span>
      <span class="pdp__modecopy">We supply a matched pair.</span>
    </button>

    {%- if has_sides_fee -%}
      <button type="button"
              class="pdp__mode"
              role="radio"
              aria-checked="false"
              data-fye-sides-mode="supplied">
        <span class="pdp__modetitle">{{ s.sides_supplied_label | default: 'Supply your own' }}</span>
        <span class="pdp__modecopy">We set your own pair.</span>
        <span class="pdp__modefee">+{{ s.sides_fee_price_pennies | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
      </button>
    {%- endif -%}

    <button type="button"
            class="pdp__mode"
            role="radio"
            aria-checked="false"
            data-fye-sides-mode="none">
      <span class="pdp__modetitle">{{ s.sides_none_label | default: 'Mount only' }}</span>
      <span class="pdp__modecopy">No side stones.</span>
    </button>
  </div>

  <input type="hidden" name="properties[Side Diamonds]" value="" data-fye-sides-prop disabled>

  {%- comment -%} ---- Mode: choose a pair ---- {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="pdp__modebody" data-fye-sides-body="required" hidden>
    <p class="pdp__choosenote">Choose the quality of your pair — priced per pair, supplied and set with your ring.</p>

    <div class="pdp__chips pdp__sidechips" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Side diamond quality">
      {%- assign rendered = 0 -%}
      {%- for entry in addons -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign parts = entry | split: '*'
          assign addon = all_products[parts[0]]
          assign quality = parts[1]

          comment
            Match this ring's spec by SKU tail. Live does the same; a code that
            has no variant on this add-on product renders no chip.
          endcomment
          assign found = nil
          for v in addon.variants
            if v.sku contains want
              assign found = v
              break
            endif
          endfor
        -%}
        {%- if found != nil and found.available -%}
          <button type="button"
                  class="pdp__chip"
                  role="radio"
                  aria-checked="false"
                  data-fye-side-qual="{{ quality | escape }}"
                  data-fye-side-variant="{{ found.id }}"
                  data-fye-side-price="{{ found.price }}"
                  data-fye-side-name="{{ addon.title | escape }}">
            <span class="pdp__chipname">{{ quality }}</span>
            <span class="pdp__chipprice">{{ found.price | money }}</span>
          </button>
          {%- assign rendered = rendered | plus: 1 -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      No chips at all means the add-on products are missing or this ring's code
      has no matching variant. Say so plainly rather than showing an empty row,
      and leave add-to-cart working — the ring is still sellable as a mount.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if rendered == 0 -%}
      <p class="pdp__hint fine">
        We do not currently hold a matched pair for this ring.
        <a href="{{ s.enquire_link | default: '/pages/contact-us' }}">Ask us to source one</a>.
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} ---- Mode: supply your own ---- {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if has_sides_fee -%}
    <div class="pdp__modebody" data-fye-sides-body="supplied" hidden>
      {%- comment -%}
        Its OWN fee product, deliberately not the centre one: the cart
        reconciler counts the centre fee by variant id and a shared line would
        be stripped.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <input type="hidden" name="properties[Setting service]" value="Customer's own side diamonds" data-fye-sides-service disabled>

      <label class="pdp__waiver">
        <input type="checkbox"
               name="properties[Waiver]"
               value="Accepted"
               data-fye-sides-waiver
               disabled>
        <span>{{ s.sides_waiver_text | default: 'I understand that stones supplied by me are set at my own risk, and that For Your Eternity cannot be held liable for damage to a stone we have not graded.' }}</span>
      </label>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
